      },
      "summary": "The Terraform tests exercise the configured alert signals and routing, but M-15's auth/scope signal is only tested by calling the telemetry helper directly. Removing the endpoint emission would leave the tests passing while real failures go unreported.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api.Tests/TelemetryPrivacyTests.cs",
          "line": 204,
          "message": "M-15 lacks a test for auth/scope alert events emitted through the application request paths; the helper-only test cannot catch a disconnected endpoint emission.",
          "confidence": 0.88,
          "category": "testing",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The M-15 test calls EmitSecurityEvent directly, while CaseEndpoints and DemoAuthEndpoints separately emit auth/scope failures from request paths. The Terraform test checks alert configuration, but no test exercises those application call sites.",
            "failureScenario": "If an endpoint stops emitting the auth/scope event, the direct helper test and Terraform alert configuration test still pass. Repeated real authentication or scope failures then produce no matching event for the alert."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
